Dux Shell (MIT, copyright 2025 Avenge Media LLC)
------------------------------------------------
view/shell/IslandTrayMenu.qml adapts the submenu stack and navigation from
quickshell/Modules/DBar/Widgets/TrayMenuContent.qml at commit
e09c2b06813d3205276167cb69e21d386c1f428f of duxlabs-dev/dux-shell.
The neutral menu tree replaces raw menu handles in the view. The full MIT
notice is in licenses/DUX-SHELL-MIT.

adapters/hyprland/HyprlandPaste.qml copies the list of terminal app ids and the
terminal rule (ends in "term" or contains "terminal") from
quickshell/Services/ClipboardService.qml (isTerminalFocused), and
view/shell/IslandClips.qml follows the key map of
quickshell/Modals/Clipboard/ClipboardKeyboardController.qml (Enter and
Shift+Enter, Ctrl+S, Delete, Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+J/K/N/P), both as installed with
DMS 2.1.0 (v2.1.0 of duxlabs-dev/dux-shell). adapters/dms/DmsClipboard.qml makes
the same socket calls as that ClipboardService (getHistory, copyEntry, the 200 ms
wait before sendPaste, deleteEntry, pinEntry/unpinEntry, getEntry, copy,
pasteSupported) and adapters/dms/DmsClipMap.js its newest-first order and the
base64 text decode of ClipboardEditor.qml. No other code is taken.

adapters/quickshell/QuickshellNotificationServer.qml,
adapters/quickshell/QuickshellNotification.qml and
adapters/quickshell/NotificationTiming.qml adapt the notification server's
arrival rules (flood guard, do-not-disturb, transient handling), the live
notification wrapper and the default showing times from
quickshell/Services/NotificationService.qml at commit
7627111c3ebd402662283f5f4a93223cda9e0a9d (v2.1.0) of duxlabs-dev/dux-shell.
Popups, grouping, history, rules and dedupe are not taken; the list is kept by
our own core.

adapters/quickshell/QuickshellOsd.qml and adapters/quickshell/OsdChange.js
follow the volume and mic OSD triggers (show on a level or mute change, a quiet
2 s after start and after our own UI sets a level) of
quickshell/Modules/OSD/VolumeOSD.qml and quickshell/Common/SessionData.qml at
v2.1.0 of duxlabs-dev/dux-shell; no code is copied. tools/dms_quiet.py writes a
local, unpublished copy of the installed DMS UI with its notification server
removed.

S6 launcher: core/matching.py and the ranking in core/launcher.py port the app
search of quickshell/Services/AppSearchService.qml (tokenize, word-boundary
match, Levenshtein fuzzy match with its typo budget, the match order and
weights, calculateFrecency's time buckets and sample size, the recency bonus)
at v2.1.0 of duxlabs-dev/dux-shell from QML/JavaScript to Python. History per
day, the one-time import and the session blocklist are ours.
adapters/quickshell/QuickshellApps.qml follows getVisibleApplications (hidden
entries out, one row per id) and launchDesktopEntry's terminal handling of
quickshell/Services/SessionService.qml at the same commit; no code is copied.

S5 equaliser: core/eq_chain.py writes a PipeWire filter-chain config whose shape
(builtin bq_peaking nodes, capture.props/playback.props) follows the example
/usr/share/pipewire/filter-chain/sink-eq6.conf shipped with PipeWire (MIT); the
graph, the mono mixers and every value are ours and no file is copied. The
response and headroom use the RBJ "Audio EQ Cookbook" peaking formulas (Robert
Bristow-Johnson; formulas, not code). The five presets are ZÆTHERION's own values.

S8 palette catalogue: adapters/common/palette_sources.py reads installed Serpantinum and DMS JSON at runtime; no theme files or upstream implementation are bundled. The Amoled Black fallback repeats the DMS colour values already used by view/ui/Design.qml (DMS MIT notice above). The ten AMOLED studies and palette picker implementation are original ZÆTHERION work.

